{"duration_api_ms":25530,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"155fcd1e-d343-434d-a14b-c899fa2be086","total_cost_usd":0.4780988,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41022,"cache_read_input_tokens":478934,"output_tokens":2706,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":943},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":569,"cache_read_input_tokens":254387,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11182},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2706,"cacheReadInputTokens":478934,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41022,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4780988,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":943,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json`. It has one row, for `egi-draft-a1v2`, and the chair is **BLANK `direction-only`**.\n\n- **The vote page:** Stratton voted Yea on SB 100 (2023) when he was in the House (\"Stratton, K.\"; \"Yeas 59 Nays 6 N/V 10\"). Under V5 option B, a record from the other chamber of the same legislature counts as `in-term`. Six No votes out of 75 members is under 10%, so the vote is `near-unanimous` and cannot carry a chair alone.\n- **The bill text:** I coded it `direction-only`. The bill stops schools from shielding a student's education record from parents. It also bans changes to that record's gender identity \"without written parental consent\".\n  - That object is the education record, not staff using \"a different name or pronouns\", so it doesn't match rung 5.\n  - It neither requires schools to \"notify parents\" (rung 4) nor limits telling them to \"when parents ask\" (rung 3).\n  - That puts Stratton on the parental-rights side, without picking a rung on that side.\n- **`needs_source`:** Stratton's own words on telling parents, and roll calls on related bills from his Senate term.\n\nHis current term dates are unknown, so code's earlier-chamber check (`prior-service-unverified` / `chamber-not-evidenced`) may flag the `in-term` code on the House vote.\n\nSeparately, some connectors need attention: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS need authorizing in claude.ai connector settings. The GitHub plugin failed to connect, and the error said its authorization header was badly formatted. None of these were needed for this task.","ttft_ms":10712,"type":"result","duration_ms":27547,"uuid":"0f8a5d4d-c2b8-43dc-96a6-bf7fabfe9539","ttft_stream_ms":1244,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1245,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
